      "anchor": {
        "mission_intent": "We need a comprehensive specification developed for our Fair Fund and Disgorgement compliance framework under Section 308 of Sarbanes-Oxley. The spec should cover the full lifecycle of how civil penalties and disgorgement proceeds are handled\u2014specifically addressing when funds are added to a disgorgement fund or Fair Fund for the benefit of injured investors versus when they're remitted to the Treasury, consistent with the SOX Section 308 exception language that modifies the default Treasury deposit requirement. The specification must incorporate a study component that reviews SEC enforcement actions involving civil penalties and disgorgements over the preceding five-year lookback window to identify where such proceedings can most efficiently and fairly provide investor restitution. Include requirements for a findings report to be delivered to the House Financial Services Committee and the Senate Banking Committee within 180 days of enactment, and ensure the spec addresses how those findings feed back into rule and regulation revisions. The report deliverable must contain a discussion of any recommended regulatory or legislative actions needed to address concerns surfaced by the study. Finally, document the methods for improving collection rates on penalties and disgorgements, and define how alternative restitution approaches should be evaluated for efficiency and fairness. Route the draft to our Office of General Counsel and SEC Liaison team for initial review by end of next quarter.",
